    "fullMarkdown": "# Mealora\n\n**A Recipe Discovery Site with an Ingredient Ordering Cart — Concept Demo**\n\nA recipe-discovery site that goes a step further than most: instead of just showing a recipe and its ingredient list, Mealora lets the user add those ingredients straight to an order — turning \"what should I cook?\" into \"what do I need to buy?\" in one flow.\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nMealora helps users go from a craving to a finished meal: search or browse recipes by ingredient, view full ingredient breakdowns, save favorites, and — the standout feature — add a recipe's ingredients directly to a priced order/cart, complete with delivery details and a running total.\n\n- **Type:** Front-end concept / portfolio project\n- **Status:** Demo — ordering and account features are front-end only; recipe data is sourced from a public recipe API\n- **Visual direction:** Warm cream background with a bold orange/red accent\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- HTML5\n- CSS3\n- JavaScript\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Home\n- Hero (\"Recipes for every craving\") with quick entry points to explore or find a specific recipe\n- **Recently Viewed** section for quick return access\n- \"Start with a familiar craving\" category shortcuts (Pizza, Chicken, Cake, Pasta, Chocolate, Breakfast)\n- \"A few delicious ideas to get you started\" — featured recipe picks\n\n### Recipe Search & Browsing\n- Free-text search plus a **\"Browse by ingredient\"** sidebar (Mushrooms, Pumpkin, Apple, Banana, Blueberry, and more) for ingredient-first discovery\n- Results grid shows recipe photo, title, and source attribution (e.g. \"The Pioneer Woman\", \"Two Peas and Their Pod\")\n\n### Recipe Detail\n- Full \"What you will need\" ingredient list with quantities\n- **Order Summary panel** — price, quantity stepper, delivery charge, delivery address, and running total\n- **Add to Cart** / **Place Order** actions, with a \"Login to Add to Cart\" gate for guests\n- Save to Favorites from the detail page\n\n### Favorites\n- Saved-recipe grid for quick access to recipes the user wants to come back to\n\n### Cart\n- \"Your Cart\" page listing saved/ordered recipes with per-item removal — effectively a grocery cart built from recipe ingredients rather than individual products\n\n### Trust & Process\n- \"A clearer way to move from idea to meal\" — a simple three-step framing: Discover, Cook, Save\n- \"Find your next favorite recipe\" call-to-action banner\n\n## Pages / Sections\n\n| Section | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| Home | Hero, recently viewed, featured picks |\n| Recipes | Search & browse-by-ingredient |\n| Recipe Detail | Ingredients + order summary |\n| Favorites | Saved recipes |\n| Cart | Ingredient-based order review |\n\n## Notes for Portfolio Presentation\n\n- Recipe content and images are sourced from a public recipe API for demo purposes; the ordering, cart, and account features are front-end only.\n- The ingredient-to-order flow (turning a recipe's ingredient list into a priced, deliverable cart) is the project's standout feature — most recipe-site clones stop at \"view recipe.\"\n- Companion video walkthrough available (`Mealora-Demo-FAST`).\n\n---\n*Documentation prepared for portfolio use — Amr Adel*\n"
