    "techStackText": "- HTML5\n- CSS3\n- JavaScript",
    "fullMarkdown": "# Savora\n\n**A Modern Food & Recipe Discovery Website — Concept Demo**\n\nA front-end recipe and food-discovery site built around bold black-and-yellow editorial styling. The focus is on making recipes easy to browse, filter, and dig into — with just enough polish (favorites, quick filtering, a newsletter capture) to feel like a real product.\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nSavora is a static demo for a recipe/food-blog style website. It combines an editorial homepage (rotating category spotlights) with a fully filterable recipe catalogue and detailed recipe pages that include ingredients, steps, and nutrition-style info.\n\n- **Type:** Front-end concept / portfolio project\n- **Status:** Demo — inventory of recipes and interactions (favorites, newsletter) are front-end only\n- **Visual direction:** High-contrast black background with bold yellow accent, editorial typography\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- HTML5\n- CSS3\n- JavaScript\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Home\n- Rotating hero banners spotlighting different categories (e.g. \"Pizza turns simple moments into rituals\", \"Desserts make the last bite matter\")\n- Quick category tabs: Burgers, Pizza, Pasta, Healthy, Desserts\n\n### Explore Categories\n- Visual category grid (Burgers, Pizza, Pasta, Healthy, Desserts, Drinks) as an entry point into the recipe catalogue\n\n### Recipe Listings\n- Filterable by category (All / Burger / Pizza / Pasta / Healthy / Dessert) and difficulty\n- Recipe cards show time, difficulty, rating, and a **View Recipe** action\n- Favorite/save toggle on each card\n\n### Popular This Week / Recipe Highlights\n- Curated \"trending\" recipe rail, separate from the main filterable grid, for editorial-style spotlighting\n\n### Recipe Detail Pages\n- Full recipe view: hero photo, prep time, difficulty, rating\n- Ingredients list\n- Step-by-step preparation instructions\n\n### Featured Recipes\n- Dedicated search-and-filter section for finding a specific recipe by name or category\n\n### Newsletter & Footer\n- \"Get Fresh Recipes Weekly\" email capture section\n- Full site footer with navigation, discovery links (Popular/Latest/Favorites), and social links\n\n## Pages / Sections\n\n| Section | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| Home | Rotating hero, category entry points |\n| Explore Categories | Visual category browse |\n| Recipes | Full filterable recipe catalogue |\n| Recipe Detail | Ingredients, steps, nutrition-style info |\n| Featured Recipes | Search & filter |\n| Newsletter | Email capture |\n\n## Notes for Portfolio Presentation\n\n- All recipes and ratings are fictional/demo content.\n- Favorites and newsletter subscription are front-end interactions only — no backend or persistence beyond the browser session.\n- Companion video walkthrough available (`Savora_Food_Demo`).\n\n---\n*Documentation prepared for portfolio use — Amr Adel*\n"
