    "techStackText": "- ASP.NET MVC 5 (.NET Framework 4.7.2)\n- C# / Razor\n- Bootstrap & JavaScript",
    "fullMarkdown": "# Skills School\n\n**A Real, Live Website for Skills Suad Kafafi International School — ASP.NET MVC 5**\n\nUnlike the concept projects elsewhere in this portfolio, this is a genuine client website: a fully built and deployed site for a real international school, currently live at **skillsschool.runasp.net**.\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nSkills School (full name: Skills Suad Kafafi International School) needed a professional web presence that could showcase its multiple curricula, academic life, achievements, and leadership to prospective and current parents. This project delivered a complete, production website covering admissions marketing, school life, staff, and contact — built and deployed for the school's real use.\n\n- **Type:** Real client project — live, in-production website\n- **Status:** Live and deployed (skillsschool.runasp.net)\n- **Visual direction:** Clean, trustworthy blue-and-white palette with real school photography throughout\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- ASP.NET MVC 5 (.NET Framework 4.7.2)\n- C# / Razor\n- Bootstrap & JavaScript\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Home\n- Hero banner (\"Graduate School of Management — Skills School\") with real building photography and a clear \"About Us\" entry point\n- Admissions announcement graphics promoting current enrollment\n\n### Accreditation & Partners\n- Four-curriculum showcase — **German School, National School, British School, American School** — communicating the range of academic pathways offered\n- Real accreditation and partner-institution logos, reinforcing over twenty years of credibility\n\n### School Stats\n- \"20 Years of Experience\" banner with real, meaningful numbers: certified teachers, successful kids, happy parents, and awards won\n\n### Our Events\n- Photo-driven event coverage (Aqua Day, National/October celebrations, end-of-year performances) giving prospective families a real feel for school life\n\n### Meet the Board & Popular Teachers\n- Individual leadership profiles (e.g. the Vice Chairman of the Board) with photo, title, and a full written bio\n- A \"Popular Teachers\" staff showcase building trust in the people behind the school\n\n### Gallery\n- Filterable photo gallery by curriculum (German / British / National / American School), with a lightbox view for full-size images\n\n### Student Life\n- **Extra-Curricular Activities** and **Performing Arts** sections detailing after-school clubs, dance, drama, music, and how students build confidence through performance\n- Curriculum filter dropdown so parents can see activities relevant to their child's track\n\n### Footer & Contact\n- Real contact details: physical address, phone numbers, and email\n- Newsletter signup and quick links to key pages (About, Contact, Privacy Policy, Terms, FAQs)\n\n## Pages / Sections\n\n| Section | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| Home | Hero & admissions entry point |\n| Accreditation | Curricula & partner credibility |\n| Events / Gallery | Photo-driven school life |\n| Meet the Board / Teachers | Leadership & staff trust |\n| Student Life | Extra-curricular & performing arts |\n| Contact / Footer | Real inquiries & location |\n\n## Notes for Portfolio Presentation\n\n- This is a **real, deployed client project** for an actual international school — not a concept or demo build. The content, photos, staff, and statistics shown are genuinely the school's own.\n- Demonstrates end-to-end delivery: design, multi-curriculum content structure, media-heavy gallery, and a live production deployment.\n- Companion video walkthrough available (`Skills-School-Demo-FAST`), recorded directly from the live site.\n\n---\n*Documentation prepared for portfolio use — Amr Adel*\n"
